e aim to invest in the  preservation of the my studies I hope it  will happen however this growing  interest has not resulted yet in the  systematic support of permanent policies  I dare to say that the main weakness  lies and the field of training training  cultural heritage should involve both  physical preservation and access  policies that balance is not happening  in Chile at the moment we do not have  any training program in conservation of  objects and collections mainly due to  the lack of funding at present there are  five university programs training in the  field of cultural heritage on a graduate  level three are part of schools  architecture and train students in the  management and conservation of built  heritage and urban planning and only two  are related to greater ship and  collections management one of them is  the program of the université de los  andes which focuses primarily on  collections curatorship and management  with the training that minds art history  documentation education marketing and  fundraising we encourage our students to  understand not only the principles  policies and practices of the discipline  but to let management tools useful the  challenge they shall face in  professional practice being aware of the  many social and educational challenges  Chile currently has and the competition  for funding between different sectors  our aim is to develop and teach good  governance principles and Beth best  practices graduates have found work in  museum states agencies culture planning  agencies historic preservation and  universities and many of them have  started their own business and managed  and management of cultural heritage as  for conservation programs we have had  two in Chile but neither of them for  sustainable and they closed  both programs managed to form a good  number of well-trained professionals  however none of them both either able to  consolidate join a teaching program and  could not establish permanent research  